  "id": "COMPOUND:15394 - PROTEIN:1493",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside is implicated in the activation of the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype through a series of molecular interactions involving Cytochrome c4, which serves as a common target for multiple compounds. This pathway is supported by the presence of multiple compounds, including 8-O-Feruloylharpagide and Quercetin 3-rutinoside-7-galactoside, all of which are linked to the same target, Cytochrome c4. The shared target of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism of action that involves the activation of the EP4 receptor, possibly through a common intermediate or pathway. The evidence from the three paths collectively highlights a convergent relationship where kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside, through its interaction with Cytochrome c4, may influence the EP4 receptor, though the exact mechanism of receptor activation remains to be elucidated. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside could play a role in modulating the EP4 receptor, potentially through a pathway involving Cytochrome c4.",
